Generated operation description:
 `regexr_transform`

The operation `regexr_transform` can be used to apply a regular expression transformation on the sponsor column. The regular expression can be designed to identify strings that contain 'dollars' or '$'. Here is an example of how the regular expression could look like:

```
\b(?:[A-Za-z0-9]+\s*){1,}?(?:dollars?|$)\b
```

This regular expression matches one or more words (including spaces) followed by either 'dollars' or '$'. The `\b` at the start and end of the pattern ensures that the match is a whole word.

The output operation would be:

```
regexr_transform(sponsor, "\b(?:[A-Za-z0-9]+\s*){1,}?(?:dollars?|$)\b")
```
